 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Sure, a complementary color is any color directly opposed to it in a color system. For chromatic full color films, it' usually green or yellow. In painting, you want avoid complements mostly for shades and tints. For instance, if you mix yellow and purple, you'll end up with green. Yes, that's one way to go. Black shadows look strong and old-fashioned, while pure white looks young and modern. You lose the value though, it looks like watercolour.",
